From 9a6bc79ac89b23f912ebaf814ec8fc04477d7aaa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 04:32:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] estuary: the player information panel after drawing it from
 its own files
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The pages were drawn on the host from the files that Kodi reads (the
generated dialog, the variables, the maps, the strings and the font of the
skin) with sample values for a Dolby Vision video that goes out native, one
that falls back to HDR10, an HDR10 one and the other pages, in English and
in the three Spanish languages, and every text that did not fit its label
was marked. What that found is fixed:

- names that were wider than their place (L3, L9, L10, L11, L254, "Drawing
  without GUI", "Enhancement layer", Spanish "Resolución de pantalla") now
  have a place that fits them, or a shorter name, or the row takes the width
  of the column with the value under its name; values that took two lines
  (the content mapping sent) wrap;
- the table of the metadata levels no longer runs under its heading;
- the panel is taller, for the longest page, and the strip with the output
  of the video is under it;
- the composer of the RPU has a row on the Dolby Vision page, and the sound
  decoded because passthrough is off says so (strings 32727, 32728, 32738,
  32739, 32816);
- the Spanish values that said "Reconstruido, enviado como HDR10" are
  shorter, and the cache has its own short name in the strip.
